Track 1: Molten Quartz Bites the Bulkhead
- Story & Context: When engineer apprentice Kaelen bypassed a life-support bus on Deck 14 to power his overloaded oscillator, the sudden electrical arc melted the inner seal of an observation viewport and flooded maintenance comms with a scorched 138 BPM drone. Ship security deployed choking riot foam into the junction, but two hundred grease-stained mechanics overwhelmed the barricade by hammering lead wrenches against vibrating pipes in time with the synth's jagged cadence. As the glass cracked under the intense heat and refracted the red warning lights into razor-sharp amber flares across the floor, Kaelen shrieked into the shipwide intercom: "We are the fuel you burn to see a sun we'll never touch!" The track’s master file was encoded into crystalline maintenance drives before Command could purge the localized power grid.
