Track 2: Cassian in the Stained-Air Lock
- Story & Context: Hidden within Sector Nine's quarantined hydroponics lab where colored mineral lights kept dead tomato vines illuminated, greenhouse operator Cassian patched an acoustic sensor to the outer airlock door to record his confession. His fingers smelled of caustic copper sulfate and burning flux as he wrenched the synth lead into an agonizing, shrill vibrato that mirrored the mechanical wheeze of his failing scrubber unit. Security monitors recorded Cassian calmly locking himself inside the de-aeration chamber, turning up his monitor amplifier until the feedback shook the bulkhead screws loose. Looking directly into the iris of the security camera, he whispered his final hook through a cracked filtration mask: "Breathe the glass we gathered, masters, and tell me if it tastes like home." The track was recovered by maintenance crews three shifts later, vibrating untouched inside the airlock's sealed data loop.
